 1s inside, or\n  - a *solid box*: all 25 cells one colour, and that colour appears in the legend.\n\n**What the demonstrations show.** Every box swaps to the other kind:\n\n- **Pattern box → solid box.** In pair 1, the box at (9,1) has the pattern `100/011/011`. Turned 180°, that is exactly the legend glyph of colour 7 (`110/110/001`). In the output, that box is solid 7. The box at (9,8) has `101/110/101`. Its transpose is the colour-4 glyph `111/010/101`, and the output box is solid 4. The box at (2,1) has `010/010/101`, which is a rotated/reflected version of glyph 2, and it becomes solid 2. So a pattern is matched to a glyph **up to rotation or reflection**, and the box is filled with that glyph's colour.\n- **Solid box → pattern box.** In pair 1, the solid-3 box at (2,8) becomes a 2-frame. Inside it is the colour-3 glyph exactly as drawn, `111/010/100`, written in 1s. Pair 3 confirms this: solid 6 becomes the colour-6 glyph unrotated, and solid 1 becomes the colour-1 glyph unrotated.\n\n**One detail to watch.** A legend glyph need not be 4-connected. In the test, glyph 4 is `110/101/110`. So I gather each glyph by colour inside the legend region, not by connected component.\n\n**Applying it to the test:**\n\n| Box | Kind | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| (1,1), pattern `111/010/111` | pattern | rotation of glyph 3 (`101/111/101`) → solid 3 |\n| (1,8), solid 6 | solid | 2-frame with glyph 6 `010/111/010` in 1s |\n| (8,1), pattern `111/101/010` | pattern | transpose of glyph 4 → solid 4 |\n| (8,8), pattern `101/110/101` | pattern | mirror of glyph 5 (`101/011/101`) → solid 5 |\n\n**How the program works.**\n\n- Background, legend colour, frame colour and pattern colour are all read from the grid, not hard-coded:\n  - the legend colour is the second-most-common colour;\n  - the frame and pattern colours come from the pattern boxes.\n- Each box is found with `objects` (multicolour) on the canvas side only.\n- One `emit` is made per converted box, and a final `emit` shows the finished grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    out = g.copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    vals, cnts = np.unique(g, return_counts=True)\n    order = [v for _, v in sorted(zip(cnts, vals), reverse=True) if v != bg]\n    lc = order[0]  # legend background colour\n    # legend region = bbox of the legend-colour component(s)\n    lcells = [(y, x) for y, x in zip(*np.where(g == lc))]\n    ly0, lx0, ly1, lx1 = bbox(lcells)\n    leg = g[ly0:ly1 + 1, lx0:lx1 + 1]\n    glyphs = {}\n    for c in np.unique(leg):\n        if c == lc:\n            continue\n        ys, xs = np.where(leg == c)\n        m = np.zeros((ys.max() - ys.min() + 1, xs.max() - xs.min() + 1), int)\n        m[ys - ys.min(), xs - xs.min()] = 1\n        glyphs[int(c)] = m\n\n    def syms(m):\n        res = []\n        for k in range(4):\n            r = np.rot90(m, k)\n            res.append(r)\n            res.append(np.fliplr(r))\n        return res\n\n    def trim(m):\n        ys, xs = np.where(m)\n        return m[ys.min():ys.max() + 1, xs.min():xs.max() + 1]\n\n    # canvas boxes\n    canvas = g.copy()\n    canvas[ly0:ly1 + 1, lx0:lx1 + 1] = bg\n    boxes = objects(canvas, bg=bg, multicolour=True)\n    frame_c, pat_c = None, None\n    for o in boxes:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        sub = g[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1]\n        if len(np.unique(sub)) > 1:\n            frame_c = int(sub[0, 0])\n            inner = sub[1:-1, 1:-1]\n            others = [v for v in np.unique(inner) if v != frame_c]\n            if others:\n                pat_c = int(others[0])\n            break\n\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Input: legend glyphs plus pattern boxes and solid boxes.\")\n    for o in boxes:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        sub = g[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1]\n        u = np.unique(sub)\n        if len(u) == 1:\n            c = int(u[0])\n            if c not in glyphs:\n                continue\n            m = glyphs[c]\n            out[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1] = frame_c\n            h, w = m.shape\n            region = out[y0 + 1:y0 + 1 + h, x0 + 1:x0 + 1 + w]\n            region[m == 1] = pat_c\n            emit(out.copy(), f\"Solid {c} box -> frame with the colour-{c} glyph drawn inside.\")\n        else:\n            inner = (sub[1:-1, 1:-1] == pat_c).astype(int)\n            if inner.sum() == 0:\n                continue\n            p = trim(inner)\n            for c, m in glyphs.items():\n                tm = trim(m)\n                if any(s.shape == p.shape and np.array_equal(s, p) for s in syms(tm)):\n                    out[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1] = c\n                    emit(out.copy(), f\"Pattern box matches glyph {c} (up to rotation/reflection) -> solid {c}.\")\n                    break\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Final output.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **A legend.** This is a strip with background 8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"It holds several small 3×3 glyphs, and each glyph has its own colour."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- a *solid box*: all 25 cells one colour, and that colour appears in the legend."}],"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Its transpose is the colour-4 glyph `111/010/101`, and the output box is solid 4."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The box at (2,1) has `010/010/101`, which is a rotated/reflected version of glyph 2, and it becomes solid 2."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"So a pattern is matched to a glyph **up to rotation or reflection**, and the box is filled with that glyph's colour."}],"instructions":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"It holds several small 3×3 glyphs, and each glyph has its own colour."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Turned 180°, that is exactly the legend glyph of colour 7 (`110/110/001`)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Its transpose is the colour-4 glyph `111/010/101`, and the output box is solid 4."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"ee4622332c7c5771d4d69d6cc32934d8107fe743a26f99801d745844363e1f71","task_sha256":"5ea2838631109751c45adc8b77f76c66f4fd080930a9024552ffec081bd97ee7","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
